'1vzs22f" />]''',
'      ,q''[    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_0kv1ra3">]''',
unistr('      ,q''[      <bpmn:text>An Opening Gateway will first look for a process variable &lt;its name&gt;:route containing a route. \00A0If not finds that, it uses that for its routing.]'''),
'      ,q''[]''',
'      ,q''[if there is no process variable, it looks for default routing]''',
'      ,q''[]''',
'      ,q''[If there is no variable and no default routing, it will return an error to the user.</bpmn:text>]''',
'      ,q''[    </bpmn:textAnnotation>]''',
'      ,q''[    <bpmn:association id="Association_0jgd1xj" sourceRef="Gateway_Three" targetRef="TextAnnotation_0kv1ra3" />]''',
'      ,q''[    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_09eif2m">]''',
unistr('      ,q''[      <bpmn:text>Method 2: Gateway Routing Expressions.\00A0]'''),
'      ,q''[]''',
unistr('      ,q''[Here we place a condition on each of the forward paths. \00A0The condition can be a PL/SQL Expression or a PL/SQL Function Body. \00A0And note that the forward paths have a Sequence Number to determine the order in which their expressions are \00A0eval')
||unistr('uated. \00A0For an Exclusive Gateway, the first path with a condition that evaluates to TRUE is chosen.]'''),
'      ,q''[]''',
unistr('      ,q''[We used a Variable Expression that evaluates ''Before Task'' in the Concept2 Task to set a process variable called ''DEPT'' equal to ''SALES''. \00A0 The demo just uses a static assignment, so it''s always ''SALES'' -- but the variable expression could ')
||'have been set by a SQL Query or a PL/SQL Function or Expression...]''',
'      ,q''[]''',
'      ,q''[Then the Condition on the Forward path uses ''bind'' syntax to compare the current value of DEPT to ''SALES'' - If so, it takes this path...]''',
'      ,q''[]''',
unistr('      ,q''[Note that we always prefix Flows for APEX variables with F4A$ - \00A0just so they don''t get confused with any APEX Page Items.]'''),
'      ,q''[]''',
'      ,q''[You could also use Substitution Syntax for a process variable, so the condition would be ''&amp;F4A$DEPT.'' = ''SALES''.]''',
'      ,q''[]''',
'      ,q''[You can re-running the process instance and try setting DEPT to ''PRODDEV'' or another value...</bpmn:text>]''',
'      ,q''[    </bpmn:textAnnotation>]''',
'      ,q''[    <bpmn:association id="Association_11qbgm5" sourceRef="Activity_Concept2" targetRef="TextAnnotation_09eif2m" />]''',
'      ,q''[  </bpmn:process>]''',
