'    pi_dgrm_name => ''Tutorial 2d - Making your process pause'',',
'    pi_dgrm_short_description => ''Flows for APEX BPMN Tutorial Series - Adding a Pause - shows how to use a timer to cause a process to pause or wait for a certain time.'',',
'    pi_dgrm_description => ''The BPMN (Business Process Model and Notation) Model "Tutorial 2D Simple Timers" is designed to provide a structured workflow for implementing and understanding timer events within business processes. This model educates u'
||'sers on integrating time-based conditions into processes using various timer configurations, ultimately improving operational efficiency and timing accuracy. Here''''s a breakdown of its key elements:',
'',
'**Start Event:**',
'',
'*   Initiates the process with the "start 2d Timers" event.',
'',
'**Adding and Specifying Timers:**',
'',
'*   **Concept 1:** Introduces the basic method of adding a timer event to pause the process for 10 seconds.',
'*   **Concept 2:** Explores specifying timers using different formats - Oracle Method and ISO 8601 Style.',
'',
'**Parallel Gateway:**',
'',
'*   Splits the process into four paths, demonstrating different timer implementations:',
'    *   **Fixed Duration (Oracle Method):**Pauses for a predetermined period using Oracle formatting.',
'    *   **Fixed Duration (ISO 8601 Style):**Utilizes ISO 8601 to specify the duration before resuming the process.',
'    *   **Fixed Time (Oracle Method):** Waits until a specific moment defined via Oracle parameters.',
'    *   **Fixed Time (ISO 8601 Method):**Specifies an exact future timestamp using ISO 8601 standards.',
'',
'**Intermediate Catch Events:**',
'',
'*   Each path leads to intermediate catch events that validate timer conditions and transition to corresponding end events.',
'',
'**End Events:**',
'',
'*   Concludes each process path after the timer conditions are met, ensuring process completion without manual oversight.',
'',
'**Documentation and Notes:**',
'',
'*   Comprehensive annotations guide users on formatting, practical applications, and future enhancements such as boundary events and message flows.',
'',
'**Value Proposition:**  ',
'This BPMN model provides businesses with a pragmatic framework to incorporate timers efficiently into their processes, enabling more precise control over operational timings. It serves as an instructive resource for educating process designers and op'
||'erators on various timer applications, ultimately enhancing process automation and reliability. By exploiting standardized and flexible timer settings, businesses can ensure processes run smoothly and on schedule, significantly optimizing resource ut'
||'ilization and process throughput.'',',
'    pi_dgrm_icon => ''fa-notebook fam-information fam-is-info'',',
'    pi_dgrm_version => ''25.1'',',
'    pi_dgrm_category => ''Tutorials'',',
'    pi_dgrm_content => l_dgrm_content',
');',
'end;',
'/',
'',
