'  flow_diagram.upload_and_parse(',
'    pi_dgrm_name => ''Tutorial 4b - Reminders and Timeouts'',',
'    pi_dgrm_short_description => ''Flows for APEX BPMN Tutorials - part 4b - shows you how to use timer boundary events to implement process timeouts and send reminders'',',
'    pi_dgrm_description => ''The "Process Tutorial 4b - Timer Boundary Events" model is a business process model that demonstrates the use of timer boundary events in workflow management. This model, designed using BPMN (Business Process Model and Not'
||'ation), highlights scenarios such as setting reminders and handling time-outs or deadlines within a business process.',
'',
'**Key Components:**',
'',
'**Non-Interrupting Timer Boundary Event:**',
'',
'*   Demonstrates how to attach a non-interrupting timer boundary event to a task which initiates a parallel path without interrupting the original task if it remains incomplete by a specified time.',
'*   Example: In this model, if the "Do Homework" task is not completed within 20 seconds, a reminder is sent while the homework task continues to be in progress.',
'',
'**Interrupting Timer Boundary Event:**',
'',
'*   Demonstrates the application of an interrupting timer boundary event, which terminates the ongoing task if not completed by the deadline and redirects the flow along an alternate path.',
'*   Example: For the "Submit Budget" task, if the budget is not submitted within 20 seconds, a default budget is automatically submitted through an interrupting timer.',
'',
'**Use Cases:**',
'',
'*   **Non-Interrupting Timers:** Ideal for scenarios requiring continuous reminders without stopping the original task, such as recurrent task reminders.',
'*   **Interrupting Timers:** Suitable for workflows requiring strict deadlines, where automatic action is needed upon timeouts, like closing submission periods.',
'',
'**Features:**',
'',
'*   Configurable timers for both interrupting and non-interrupting events.',
'*   The ability to set repetitive triggers for non-interrupting timers.',
'*   Instructional annotations for understanding the purpose and application of timer events in processes.',
'',
'**Application in Business Processes:**',
'',
'*   This model can be used as a training tool to educate process designers about implementing time-based control in business workflows.',
'*   It can also serve as a template for developing business processes requiring automated reminders and deadline management, ensuring efficiency and timeliness.',
'',
'Overall, the Process Tutorial 4b model serves as an insightful example for businesses aiming to implement effective process management with the use of timer boundary events to optimize task completion and time management.'',',
'    pi_dgrm_icon => ''fa-notebook fam-information fam-is-info'',',
'    pi_dgrm_version => ''25.1'',',
'    pi_dgrm_category => ''Tutorials'',',
'    pi_dgrm_content => l_dgrm_content',
');',
'end;',
