'      ,q''[In this diagram, the Sales &amp; Marketing Group have just created a sales promotion process to call targeted customers, and try to sell them a product.]''',
'      ,q''[If the sales call is successful, they will take an order - and ship the product to the customer.]''',
'      ,q''[]''',
unistr('      ,q''[The Sales and Marketing Group don''t want to define all of the order processing process steps in their promotion. \00A0 But the Supply Chain IT developers have already created a process for booking an order, picking, packing, and shipping it. \00A0T')
||unistr('his Shipping process is contained in the model ''Tutorial 5e''. \00A0 So our Sales and Marketing process developer can just ''call'' this model using a Call Activity (Task ''Process Order'')</bpmn:text>]'''),
'      ,q''[    </bpmn:textAnnotation>]''',
