'      ,q''[    <bpmn:textAnnotation id="TextAnnotation_1aazt0j">]''',
unistr('      ,q''[      <bpmn:text>The Call Activity calls another diagram. (Tutorial 5e). \00A0Look at theProperties Panel to see how this is configured.]'''),
'      ,q''[]''',
unistr('      ,q''[When configuring a Call Activity call, first find the model you want to call. \00A0Select a specific version, or the latest version.]'''),
'      ,q''[]''',
unistr('      ,q''[Use the In/Out Variables tab to configure how process variables in the Calling diagram get copied into the Called Diagram. \00A0Click on the green ''Load Defined Variables'' button to get all of the required Input and Output Variables loaded into')
||' the properties panel....]''',
'      ,q''[]''',
'      ,q''[Process Variables are scoped to a single diagram -- so any variables in the calling diagram only exist in the called diagram if you copy them into the called diagram when the diagram starts running.]''',
'      ,q''[]''',
'      ,q''[Similarly, any variables or results that you create in the called diagram need be explicitly returned to the calling diagram when election of the called diagram completes.</bpmn:text>]''',
'      ,q''[    </bpmn:textAnnotation>]''',
