'    pi_dgrm_name => ''Tutorial 7e - Introduction to Iterations and Tasks'',',
'    pi_dgrm_short_description => ''Flows for APEX BPMN Tutorial - Part 7e - introduces multi-instance tasks and BPMN loops.  This is an Enterprise Edition only feature.'',',
'    pi_dgrm_description => ''The business model provided is a workflow process diagram created using Business Process Model and Notation (BPMN). This model outlines a comprehensive overview of a workflow utilizing loops and iterators within a business'
||' process. Here''''s a brief summary of the business workflow:',
'',
'**Initialization (Start Event)**: The process begins with a "Start" event, triggering the subsequent tasks in the workflow.',
'',
'**Pre-Split Task (Activity\_PreSplit)**: The initial task, "Pre-Split," prepares the process for subsequent splitting into parallel or sequential tasks.',
'',
'**Parallel Workflow Branching (Gateway\_Split)**: The workflow is split into parallel paths using a parallel gateway. Each path represents different sections of a process executed concurrently.',
'',
'**Task Sequences**:',
'',
'**Sequence A (List Processing)**:',
'',
'*   "A1-List": Retrieves a list of employee names from a department into a process variable.',
'*   "A2": Iterates over the list sequentially until a certain condition is met.',
'*   "A3": Finalizes actions on the list items.',
'',
'**Sequence B (Array Processing)**:',
'',
'*   "B1-Array": Retrieves employee details as JSON data (an array) into a process variable.',
'*   "B2": Iterates over the JSON array in parallel until a condition is fulfilled.',
'*   "B3": Processes each JSON item separately.',
'',
'**Sequence C (Direct Query Processing)**:',
'',
unistr('*   "C1-Query": Rather than creating a variable in this step, we go straight to C2\2026'),
'*   "C2": Executes a database query to directly retrieve employee details , and uses the query result in parallel, again until a certain completion condition is achieved.',
'*   "C3": Finalizes the handling of query results.',
'',
'**Sequence D (Loop Processing)**:',
'',
'*   "D1-Loop": Initiates a looping process.',
'*   "D2": Continues the loop until a specified condition is met.',
'*   "D3": Final processing after the loop completes.',
'',
'**End Events**: Each sequence concludes with an "End" event, marking the completion of the respective process branch.',
'',
'**Annotations**: Descriptive text annotations provide insights into each task and sequence, explaining the nature and requirements of iterations and loops.',
'',
'This process model shows a structured approach to manage workflows using iterations, loops, and parallel processing, ideal for systems where tasks need to be executed in sequences or loops based on the conditions derived from queries or lists. It is '
||'noted that the use of iterations and loops requires an Enterprise Edition setup, ensuring scalability and robustness in complex business scenarios.'',',
'    pi_dgrm_icon => ''fa-notebook fam-information fam-is-info'',',
'    pi_dgrm_version => ''25.1'',',
'    pi_dgrm_category => ''Tutorials'',',
'    pi_dgrm_content => l_dgrm_content',
');',
'end;',
